Subject: videotoolbox: a real-time frame's packet comes with the frame

The encoder's packets were read without waiting right after the frame was
given, while VideoToolbox encodes on a thread of its own: each packet came
out when the next frame was sent, a frame time late. In real time and with
no B frames the frame is completed first.

---
 libavcodec/videotoolboxenc.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/videotoolboxenc.c b/libavcodec/videotoolboxenc.c
--- a/libavcodec/videotoolboxenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/videotoolboxenc.c
@@ -2723,6 +2723,20 @@
     if (!get_frame) {
         status = 0;
         goto end_nopkt;
+    }
+
+    // Real time, frames in order: the frame's packet is asked for now.
+    // VideoToolbox gives it a few ms later on a thread of its own, and what is
+    // read below without waiting was the packet of the frame before: every
+    // packet came out a frame time late (17 ms at 60 fps, 33 ms at 30).
+    if (frame && vtctx->realtime > 0 && !vtctx->has_b_frames) {
+        status = VTCompressionSessionCompleteFrames(vtctx->session,
+                                                    kCMTimeInvalid);
+        if (status) {
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Error completing frame: %d\n", status);
+            status = AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
+            goto end_nopkt;
+        }
     }
 
     status = vtenc_q_pop(vtctx, !frame, &buf, &sei);
